We're hiring for this role at either the Architect I ($130k-144k) or Architect II ($151k-165k) level, depending on the experience and independence a candidate brings. Level differences are outlined below. &nbsp;

About the Role &nbsp;

Nightingale College is looking for a Solutions Architect who thinks in systems, builds with AI, and owns a problem from the first conversation all the way to production. This isn't a traditional developer role - you won't be handed a spec and told to code it. You'll talk directly with the people who have the problem, design a solution that actually fits, and use AI-native tools as your primary build engine to bring it to life. If you're energized by eliminating the gap between "here's what we need" and "here's a working solution," this role was built for you. &nbsp;

What You'll Do &nbsp;

• Engage directly with end-users and stakeholders to understand problems, surface requirements, and define what success looks like.

• Design solution architectures that are practical, scalable, and grounded in real business needs.

• Build and iterate on solutions using AI-native development tools and workflows.

• Own your solution from first conversation through production deployment.

• Continuously shrink the time between spotting a problem and shipping working software.

• Spot opportunities to improve existing systems and workflows through AI-enabled solutions.

What You Bring &nbsp;

• Experience in a solutions, technical, product, or systems role (see level breakdown below).

• A demonstrated ability to build working solutions using AI-native tools - this is required in place of a formal degree.

• Comfort listening first and building second: you gather requirements by asking questions, not assuming answers.

• A systems-thinking mindset - you see the whole problem, not just the immediate ask.

• An iterative approach: you ship early, gather feedback, and improve fast.

• Strong communication skills that bridge business needs and technical reality.

• Relevant cloud, data, or AI platform certifications are a plus, though not required.

Level Differences:

&nbsp;

Architect I &nbsp;

Architect II &nbsp;

Scope &nbsp;

Assigned, well-defined problems &nbsp;

Moderately complex, cross-functional problems &nbsp;

Autonomy &nbsp;

Guided &nbsp;

Independent, with check-ins &nbsp;

Day-to-Day &nbsp;

Works on clearly scoped problems under close guidance; participates in user conversations with support from senior team members &nbsp;

Independently gathers requirements through direct end-user engagement; manages full delivery cycle with limited oversight; identifies gaps and proposes improvements; contributes to team standards and shares learnings &nbsp;

&nbsp; Minimum Qualifications by Level:

&nbsp;

Architect I &nbsp;

Architect II &nbsp;

Experience &nbsp;

0-2 years in a solutions, technical, product, or systems role &nbsp;

2-4 years in a solutions, technical, product, or systems role &nbsp;

AI-Building Track Record &nbsp;

Demonstrated ability to build working solutions with AI-native tools &nbsp;

Proven track record of delivering AI-built solutions end-to-end &nbsp;

&nbsp; What We're Not Looking For &nbsp;

• Traditional developers who just use AI to write code faster.

• Specialists who design but don't build, or build but don't design.

• Someone who needs a fully-scoped spec before they can start.

Why Nightingale &nbsp;

Nightingale College is a high-impact community, not just a workplace. We believe the future of software delivery belongs to people who can think in systems, talk to humans, and build with AI - all in the same motion. This is a remote role with flexibility, built around core collaboration hours in Mountain Time, with travel required just once a year. If you want to build things that matter and grow your craft while doing it, we'd love to talk.
Budgeted Hiring Range
$130,000 &mdash; $165,000 USD

